        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The reduction in unplanned downtime alone saved [ORG_2] an estimated EUR 1.3 million in the first year. The investment in sensors, gateways and software paid for itself within seven months. In addition, components are now replaced based on their actual condition rather than at fixed intervals, which has reduced spare parts costs by almost a quarter."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\"The biggest change is in the way we work,\" says [PERSON_1]. \"Our technicians now plan their week instead of running from one breakdown to the next. That has also made the job more attractive for young skilled workers.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What's Next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Encouraged by these results, [ORG_2] plans to extend condition monitoring to the melting furnaces and the cooling water circuits in 2027. The next step will be the use of energy consumption data to further reduce downtime caused by overheating and to optimise the energy efficiency of the foundry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Would you like to find out how condition monitoring can reduce downtime in your production? Read more about the solution on our "
          },
          {
